<%- include('partials/header', {title: 'WordPress CI/CD with CodePipeline'}) %>

<section class="project-hero">
  <a href="/" class="project-back-btn"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  <h1>WordPress CI/CD with AWS CodePipeline & CloudFormation</h1>
  <p>Automated WordPress deployment using CodePipeline integrated with GitHub, powered by CloudFormation for infrastructure provisioning.</p>
  <div class="project-hero-tags">
    <span>CodePipeline</span><span>CloudFormation</span><span>GitHub</span><span>CI/CD</span><span>EC2</span>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="project-details">
  <div class="center">
    <img src="/images/codepipeline.png" alt="WordPress CI/CD Pipeline Architecture" class="project-diagram">
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Project Overview</h3>
    <p>This project demonstrates a <strong>CI/CD pipeline</strong> for WordPress on AWS — every GitHub commit automatically triggers CodePipeline, which provisions/updates infrastructure via CloudFormation.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Source:</strong> GitHub repo with WordPress app and CloudFormation templates.</li>
      <li><strong>Pipeline:</strong> AWS CodePipeline triggering on every commit.</li>
      <li><strong>Infrastructure:</strong> CloudFormation provisioning EC2, MySQL, Apache, PHP, and WordPress.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Architecture Explanation</h3>
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🔄 CI/CD Flow</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>GitHub</strong> — Source & webhook trigger</li>
          <li><strong>CodePipeline</strong> — Orchestrates deployment</li>
          <li><strong>S3</strong> — Pipeline artifact storage</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🏗️ Infrastructure</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>CloudFormation</strong> — Provisions all resources</li>
          <li><strong>EC2</strong> — Hosts Apache, PHP, MySQL, WordPress</li>
          <li><strong>Security Group</strong> — HTTP (80) and SSH (22)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Key Learnings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Set up <strong>GitHub → AWS CodePipeline</strong> integration with webhooks.</li>
      <li>Created IAM roles for <strong>CodePipeline and CloudFormation</strong> with correct permissions.</li>
      <li>Observed how CodePipeline fetches changes from GitHub and <strong>redeploys automatically</strong>.</li>
      <li>Understood the importance of <strong>Infrastructure as Code and CI/CD</strong> combined.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Notes & Best Practices</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Use <strong>Amazon RDS</strong> instead of local MySQL for production scalability.</li>
      <li>Add <strong>Auto Scaling + Load Balancer</strong> for high availability.</li>
      <li>Use <strong>separate pipelines</strong> for staging and production environments.</li>
      <li>Store sensitive values in <strong>AWS Secrets Manager</strong>, never in templates.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="center">
    <a href="/" class="btn-back"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  </div>
</div>

